    "title": "When is the Final Four? Time, channel and streaming for March Madness",
    "text": "Updated March 29, 2026, 8:37 p.m. ETWe're down to four, and that means we have TV times.The Final Four of the 2026 NCAA Tournament is set, with four teams vying for a place in the national championship in their national semifinal games on Saturday, April 4, at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis. The first game will tip off at 6 p.m. ET and the second game will go at approximately 8:49 p.m ET (or 25 minutes after the first game ends, if it goes long).South 3-seed Illinois and East 2-seed Connecticut will play in the night's first game, followed by 1-seed Arizona and 1-seed Michigan basketball as the nightcap.Watch NCAA Tournament on Sling TVOne of the Final Four matchups will be a battle of 1-seeds, as Michigan basketball takes on Arizona in one of the two national semifinal games. The other game will be between 3-seed Illinois and the winner of the Duke-UConn East regional final, tipping off later today.Michigan beat 6-seed Tennessee in the Midwest regional final on Sunday, March 29, to get this point, while Arizona beat 2-seed Purdue, 79-64, on Saturday, March 28, to make the Final Four.Here's what you need to know about the Final Four schedule.Michigan basketball vs Arizona NCAA March Madness Final Four timeDate: Saturday, April 4.Time: 8:49 p.m. ET.Location: Lucas Oil Stadium, Indianapolis.Michigan basketball vs Arizona NCAA March Madness Final Four channelTipoff: 8:49 p.m. ET.Channel: TBS.Streaming: Sling TV.Both of Saturday's Final Four matchups can be watched on TBS and streamed on Sling TV.Watch NCAA Tournament on Sling TVNeed to catch up on the news during your lunch break? Sign up for our Sports Briefing newsletter to get daily summaries of Detroit sports! You can reach Christian at cromo@freepress.com.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
